========================================================================================
PART 3 -- TRIG-MOMENT (TOEPLITZ) VIEW + FLAT EXTENSION (Curto-Fialkow)
========================================================================================
The lonely measure mu = uniform on the extremal atoms. Its Fourier moments y_k = (1/|A|) sum_a e^{-2pi i k a}
form a Toeplitz matrix M_K=[y_{j-l}] that is PSD (Bochner) with rank = #atoms (Caratheodory-Toeplitz).

construction: #atoms=2  Toeplitz M_K rank -> stabilizes at 2 (=#atoms? True)
  rank(M_K) for K=1,5,10,20,30: 2, 2, 2, 2, 2
  min eigenvalue over K (PSD/Bochner, should be >= ~0): -2.27e-14   flat-extension rank stable from K>=1
  localization: every atom is lonely for every v in S (||va|| >= M): True  (=> mu is a lonely measure)

AP {1..13}: #atoms=6  Toeplitz M_K rank -> stabilizes at 6 (=#atoms? True)
  rank(M_K) for K=1,5,10,20,30: 2, 6, 6, 6, 6
  min eigenvalue over K (PSD/Bochner, should be >= ~0): -1.11e-14   flat-extension rank stable from K>=5
  localization: every atom is lonely for every v in S (||va|| >= M): True  (=> mu is a lonely measure)

========================================================================================
PART 4 -- WHY NO FINITE LEVEL IS EXACT: the atom needs degree ~ denominator(t*) (uncertainty)
========================================================================================
Resolving a spike at t* of denominator D needs Fourier degree ~ D (uncertainty / Nyquist).
So the moment relaxation must reach degree ~ Phi6(n) to 'see' the atom. Numerology vs lazy-cut #cuts:
  n=8: Phi6=57  t*=n/Phi6=8/57 denom=57  (lazy-cut n=12 closed at ~208 cuts; degree scale ~ Phi6)
  n=10: Phi6=91  t*=n/Phi6=10/91 denom=91  (lazy-cut n=12 closed at ~208 cuts; degree scale ~ Phi6)
  n=12: Phi6=133  t*=n/Phi6=12/133 denom=133  (lazy-cut n=12 closed at ~208 cuts; degree scale ~ Phi6)
  n=14: Phi6=183  t*=n/Phi6=14/183 denom=183  (lazy-cut n=12 closed at ~208 cuts; degree scale ~ Phi6)

=> finite moment level = klein's Delsarte LP (HYP-3784, near-tight at bounded V, gapped as V grows);
   the gap is HYP-3785's spectral gap = the moment-hierarchy face of S61 'finite-D cannot close Step 3'.
DONE.
